WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.990 align:start position:0%
 
i'm ella yakubovska  i work as a policy and campaigns officer  at european digital rights  and i'm one of the coordinators of the  reclaim your face campaign to  ban biometric mass surveillance in  europe my name is gregory ingles  i'm from the european citizen initiative  freedom to share  it's an initiative targeted to changing  the copyright rules  to allow free sharing of copyrighted  material  and at the same time to reimburse the  authors  in a fair way so  hi so my name is shanet o'keefe and i'm  a member of the voters at borders  european citizens initiative  it doesn't make sense to me that you can  move to another country and you can  live in that society i don't know if you  have children you send your children to  school there  you work there you pay taxes you go to  the hospitals there  you take part in the community you  become part of the community you're in a  sports team there  and you can't vote it doesn't make sense  to me  we were really drawn to the fact that  the european citizens initiative  allows us to potentially influence eu  legislation  that's a massive thing and you know  sometimes the  eu can seem kind of remote to people and  it's not always clear how the eu's work  connects to people's lives so  the european citizens initiative being a  process that  anyone can launch and that requires the  signatures of  one million people means that it's it's  it's really broad it's a really great  way of engaging people  that might not realize that they  actually have a chance to influence the  laws that the eu creates  there could be some alternatives rather  than starting a european citizen  initiative one could run  a protest in the streets and and and  make a  simple petition but we saw that back in  2019  as we had organized a wave of protest in  the streets  protesting against the article 13 of the  new european copyright directive  that this protest basically um  not only went unheard by politicians but  actually been  actually mocked from from the top and  said like these are googlebots  and you cannot take them seriously so  we looked what is the instrument how we  can make ourselves  be taken seriously and by making  european citizen initiative  we are addressing directly the  commission and if we are successful  they need to be taken seriously looking  at  the different tools of direct democracy  available in the eu  we've we've looked at petitions and  lobbying  lobbying lobbying governments lobbying  the  institutions but we've seen that the eci  tool is the best  tool especially for young people to get  involved in and  yeah directly get involved in eu policy  making  when we first started the process of  getting our european citizens initiative  registered i think we hadn't fully  appreciated  the complexity of the process because  this is a  legally recognized process and you have  to  take care in how you write your proposal  and how you submit it so my biggest  takeaway really  is to get as much advice early on as you  possibly can  there are some really brilliant  resources out there through the  european citizens initiative forum and  once we started  taking advantage of those it got a lot  easier the way to register european  citizen initiative is long  and we had very fast found a team of  people across europe  from seven different countries that was  the easiest part  the complicated part was to write the  legal text  that is actionable upon so that has been  accepted by the european commission  and also to do all the administrative  tasks  with the new regulation it was great  because we didn't have to launch our eci  the second  that we had been accepted by the  commission we were able to take some  time to actually  build up partnerships um before we  launched so we launched september 1st  on 2020 and we had been accepted our  proposals have been accepted in march so  there was a really nice  gap that we could you know build up the  team and do a lot of research  and that's also where the eci form came  in because we did ask them i get a lot  of advice from them  about um kind of legal grounds and how  to  build up our strategy one of the  challenges that we faced when we were  seeking to register  our european citizens initiative was  which treaty basis could be the the  legal basis for  the demand that we were putting forward  to the commission and  as a group of citizen organizers that's  something that we weren't  100 comfortable with ourselves so  actually being able to  turn to the european citizens initiative  forum and ask for their advice  their legal advice was really really  powerful and made the difference with  the things that we weren't not sure  about  and they were able to give us some  recommendations  on on the legal basis for our ask that  led  to our initiative being registered in  the end  the problem to actually register the  official text  to submit it to european commission so  it can be translated and everything  this was complicated and also to have  the it set up was  quite complicated task even that we  felt that we know what we're doing but  if we would do it differently this time  i we would rather start with building up  a support network  and get more organizations on start  our experience with the commission's  signature collection website has been  very positive  when you click onto it you click i think  it's support voters without borders  initiative  and you can see how signature collection  in each country is going  um which is very good you can see the  the threshold the amount of signatures  that has to be collected in that country  so the threshold we call it  and the percentage of that that has been  reached  campaigning at any time is a challenging  thing trying to mobilize people  and translate at least for us what is  quite a  heavy policy message into something that  helps people  understand why this topic actually  impacts their day-to-day life  so we've had to think quite creatively  about how we can  get some of our content to be picked up  and  to kind of go viral so to speak um  on social media and one of the things  that we found that  is really really effective is to hook  what it is that we're campaigning for  onto things that are happening in the  news because that is where people seem  to be  most interested you're watching this  video so you obviously have found the  forum  and this is a good thing because i took  some days to find it  as i was in the beginning to starting  the european citizen initiative  and i could use some of the material  in this forum much earlier  a few people mentioned it to me at the  beginning that this is a lot of work  and i think it was quite difficult for  me to really  understand what that meant but in in  practice i think just being aware that  you really need to put in the time to  get a good effect with your european  citizens initiatives so at the beginning  making sure that you've understood all  of the obligations that are  on you and putting a lot of time and  effort into making sure that your  proposal  is within the the legal competence of  the european commission and seeking  advice to help you on that  um making sure that you've thought about  it not just from  the perspective of the european  commission but also people that are then  going to sign it  one last piece of advice that i could  give reach out to other people who are  running  european citizen initiative at this time  or have  done it previously because you can  actually support  each other and you can also profit  from experience and learn and also  don't be afraid we are all in the same  boat  you

